---
# High-signal, low-noise static analysis for the hand-written C of the extension.
# Only our own files are reported (HeaderFilterRegex); the generated protobuf-c
# bindings are never passed to clang-tidy. Checks that only fire as false
# positives on this codebase are disabled deliberately:
#   - security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling: flags every memcpy/
#     memset and suggests the C11 Annex K *_s functions, which do not exist on
#     glibc — pure noise.
#   - core.NullDereference: fires on every PHP method because the analyzer cannot
#     know Zend's getThis() is non-null in a method body (and emalloc never
#     returns NULL); on this code it produces only false positives.
#   - the bugprone-* exclusions are false positives from Zend's emalloc/efree
#     macro expansions or the established PHP-extension "_pinba_*" struct-tag idiom.
#   - readability-identifier-length: idiomatic short C names (loop counters i/j,
#     qsort comparator a/b, the timer t/u/sa/fd locals) plus the _i/_t/_z/_s/_p
#     temporaries injected by Zend's ZEND_HASH_FOREACH_* macros, which are not
#     ours to rename — pure noise on this codebase.
#   - readability-function-cognitive-complexity: the request-packet builders and
#     tag/timer marshalling functions are intentionally large, branch-heavy units
#     mirroring the wire format; "fixing" them means rewriting a released
#     extension at real risk of regression. Reported as info, not enforced here.
#   - cert-dcl37-c / cert-dcl51-cpp: duplicate of bugprone-reserved-identifier
#     above — they flag the same "_pinba_*" struct-tag idiom, already accepted.
# cert-* and google-* are enabled purely as zero-cost regression guards: they
# currently produce no findings on our files, so they only fire if a future
# change introduces, e.g., an unchecked dangerous-API return or an unsafe cast.
Checks: >
  -*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -clang-analyzer-core.NullDereference,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-reserved-identifier,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion,
  -bugprone-narrowing-conversions,
  portability-*,
  concurrency-*,
  cert-*,
  -cert-dcl37-c,
  -cert-dcl51-cpp,
  google-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '(^|/)(pinba\.c|php_pinba\.h)$'
...
